{"id": "DfHkekdRm9r", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why was Parshurama, a sage's grandson, born a fierce WARRIOR? Because two bowls of sacred kheer got SWAPPED. 🍚🪓\n\nSage Richika wanted to marry Princess Satyavati. Her father, King Gadhi, asked for 1,000 moon-white horses, each with ONE black ear, sure he'd fail. Richika got them from Varuna, lord of the waters.\n\nSatyavati and her mother both wanted a son, so Richika made two bowls of charu (sacred kheer): one would give a calm, wise sage (for his wife), the other a mighty warrior (for her mother). While he went to bathe, the mother thought, \"His wife's bowl must be better,\" and the two swapped.\n\nRichika knew at once: \"Your son will be a fierce warrior.\" Satyavati begged, and he let it pass to her GRANDSON instead. Her son Jamadagni was born a calm sage, and his son was Parshurama, the brahmin with a warrior's fire, Vishnu's sixth avatar.\n\nThe twist: her mother's son became VISHVAMITRA, the king who became a sage. One bowl swapped. Two legends. 🙏\n\n📖 Sources: Bhagavata Purana 9.15, Vishnu Purana 4.7, Mahabharata 12.49.\n\nThis is Part 1 of our Parshurama series. Every part stands on its own, so start anywhere!\n\n📚 Kids' picture books on the Navadurga: Books 1–3, set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💬 Comment \"JAI PARSHURAM\" 🙏\n🔁 Share it with someone who loves kheer!\n📌 Save it for story time.\n\n#parshurama #parashurama #vishnuavatar #dashavatar #hindumythology #sanatandharma #puranas #bhagavatapurana #vishvamitra #indianmythology #storiesforkids #hindustories #mythologystories #rishikatha #jaiparshuram", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793362967, "like_count": 6576, "comment_count": 48, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-3040111802995484a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 51.831, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcod